RADIO: The time is 5:53 PM. Before our evening bulletin, a local reminder from the District Air Defense Command: [next=2]

Blackout curtains must be drawn at dusk, and harbour lights will be reduced after six. The evening ferries and postal collections will continue as scheduled. [next=2.5]

RADIO: Moving to regional defense... The general air-raid alert for the Kiyoshima district is now a light advisory. [next=2]

Radar reports a single high-altitude enemy plane approaching from the east. Command believes it is a weather flight. Anti-aircraft guns will stand down and shelters will remain closed. [next=2.5]

RADIO: So don't worry, folks. Right now I'd be more concerned about the old Gojira (Godzilla) stories than one lonely plane in the clouds. Stay alert, but there is no immediate danger. [next=1.8]

=> END